## Build 3c — STEP toward few-ms lensed lnlike. Root cause (measured): within one LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood.lnlike the Chang-Refsdal engine evaluates ~100 coarse w-nodes; ~1.9 ms/node is operator._contract_orders (an order-40 sum of 85x85 complex bilinear forms), i.e. ~190 ms of the ~300 ms eval. Because lens params are FIXED within one lnlike and only w varies, the monomial power vectors (z_powers, zbar_powers), the operator `table`, and the derivative gather map half_sum are ALL w-independent. The Professor derived a WEIGHT-VECTOR REDUCTION: precompute per order a length-85 complex vector v_order[j] = scatter-add of z_powers[a]*table[order,a,b]*zbar_powers[b] over the fixed index map idx(a,b)=clamp(half_sum[a,b]+order) (via np.add.at); then each node's order-n contribution is a single length-85 dot v_order.derivs_scaled[node] instead of an 85x85 bilinear form. This is ~190x on the contraction (190 ms -> ~1 ms across all nodes) and is NOT a naive (n_nodes,85,85) BLAS tensor (which keeps the full FLOP count, only ~5-10x). WP1 implements this in operator.py behind a batched entry point F_op_grid(w_array, y, gamma, ...) that computes the shared quantities ONCE, runs a batched njit core, applies all four F005 named refusals per node with BYTE-FROZEN thresholds, and returns a lean (values, orders, converged); scalar F_op delegates to F_op_grid([w]) so there is ONE contraction path and ONE certification (Professor + Simplifier). WP2 wires channels._exact_total to call F_op_grid once on the wave-branch node subset (geometric-branch nodes unchanged, per-node phase exp(-1j*w*t_min) preserved). PREDICTED FLOOR (arithmetic): contraction ~2 ms + 1F1 kernel ~35 ms (not batchable: variable n_terms + sequential dd) + overhead ~1 ms + non-engine ~70 ms = ~108 ms, a ~2.9x lnlike reduction. The timing gate is set to that arithmetic-derived floor (MS_CEILING = 0.175 s = 108 ms x 1.6 margin), REPLACING the machine-calibrated 0.5 s; the hard machine-independent gate SPEEDUP_MIN rises 3.0 -> 8.0 (predicted lnlike ~139x over brute). This build does NOT reach 10 ms; the named next lever is Lever B — a 3D post-contraction surrogate of the smooth O(1) channel kernels K_a over the reduced lens space (w, y' in shear frame, gamma'), deferred to Build 4 (it is materially different from the rejected 2D derivative-ladder table because it tabulates the O(1) post-contraction output, not the ~100-decade internal ladder). Lever D (ODE marching) rejected as more expensive at 100 nodes; Lever C (fewer nodes) dropped (saves <0.5 ms after WP1 and would re-touch the 3b accuracy gate). ASSUMPTIONS documented: node count is ~100 (the brief's phrasing was clarified by the Professor); non-engine ~70 ms (caustic + spline + RB summary + candidate-ratio waveform co-cost) is out of scope and becomes the new bottleneck, named in the change report.

### WP1: Weight-vector batched contraction + single-path F_op_grid in operator.py
  What: Replace the per-node 85x85 bilinear contraction with the weight-vector reduction and expose a batched engine entry point that evaluates the whole wave-branch w-node grid in one call, preserving the F005 certified-or-named-refusal contract exactly. Do NOT write any tests (the Test Developer authors all tests).
  Where: cogwheel/lensing/chang_refsdal/operator.py (_contract_orders, F_op, module __all__; new F_op_grid and a batched njit core).
  How: ALGEBRA (Professor, authoritative): within one lnlike the lens params are fixed and only w varies, so z_powers, zbar_powers, the operator `table`, half_sum, y_scaled, gamma_scaled, s and dim are w-INDEPENDENT. For each order n precompute a length-`dim` complex weight vector v_n where v_n[j] = sum over all (a,b) with idx(a,b)==j of z_powers[a]*table[n,a,b]*zbar_powers[b], and idx(a,b) = min(half_sum[a,b]+n, dim-1) (the SAME clamp the current kernel uses). Build v_n with a scatter-add (np.add.outer/np.add.at or an explicit accumulation) — no new class (Simplifier). Also precompute the all-positive companion vector v_abs_n[j] from |z_powers[a]|*|table[n,a,b]|*|zbar_powers[b]| for the positive_total/max_term bookkeeping. Then per node the order-n contribution is the single length-`dim` dot v_n . derivs_scaled[node] (and abs-dot for the positive companion), replacing the 85x85 double loop; multiply by the per-node, per-order coeff = prod(1j*gamma_scaled/(2*w[node]*order)). SIGNATURE: add F_op_grid(w_array, y, gamma, *, beta=0.0, kappa=0.0, max_order=MAX_ORDER) -> (values: complex ndarray, orders: int ndarray, converged: bool ndarray). It (1) computes the mass-sheet map, table, z/zbar powers, half_sum, and the {v_n, v_abs_n} weight vectors ONCE; (2) for each node computes derivs = point_mass_g_derivatives(w[node], s, ...) (KERNEL IS NOT BATCHED — variable n_terms per node), the per-node power-of-two scale_exp via np.frexp/np.ldexp EXACTLY as today, then the batched njit contraction core returning per-node (total, positive_total, max_term, order_used, last_ratio, converged); (3) applies ALL FOUR refusals per node with UNCHANGED thresholds and messages (non-finite total; max_term/|total| > _CANCELLATION_REFUSAL; estimated_tail > _CONTRACTION_TARGET; _CONTRACTION_UNIT_ROUNDOFF*(positive_total/|total|) > _CONTRACTION_GUARD), and the per-node mass-sheet + phase reconstruction (ldexp back by the node's own scale_exp, exp(0.5j*w*log(lam)-...), /lam) — every constant BYTE-FROZEN, per FINDINGS F005/F001. RETURN LEAN (Simplifier trim): only (values, orders, converged); the refusal quantities are intermediates that raise-or-not, NOT return fields. Refactor scalar F_op(w, ...) to a thin wrapper: value, = F_op_grid(np.asarray([w]), ...)[0-slot] and reconstruct its (value, OperatorDiagnostics) return so there is ONE contraction path and ONE certification (Professor: avoids a value/refusal coherence bug). The batched njit core must be numba-njit fastmath=False; keep all raising/thresholds/scipy-loggamma in Python. GATHER-INDEX INVARIANT to honor (Inspector idiom): idx clamps to dim-1 and out-of-range table cells carry a zero coefficient, so clamped lookups never contribute wrongly. NUMERICAL NOTE (Professor): the accumulation-order change (blocked/dot vs current column-then-row) is SAFE inside the certified band — for returned points condition = positive_total/|total| < ~9e6 so the perturbation is < ~2e-8 relative, ~200x under the 1e-10 target; higher-condition points are already refused. Add F_op_grid to __all__.
  Who: Coder
  Verification: operator.py exposes F_op_grid(w_array, y, gamma, *, beta, kappa, max_order) returning (values, orders, converged); scalar F_op delegates to it (a single-element grid call) so exactly one contraction implementation exists. The contraction uses the weight-vector reduction (per-order length-dim v_n scatter-add dotted against per-node derivs_scaled), not an 85x85 per-node bilinear form and not an (n_nodes,dim,dim) tensor. All four F005 refusals fire per node with the four thresholds (_CANCELLATION_REFUSAL, _CONTRACTION_TARGET, _CONTRACTION_GUARD, _CONTRACTION_UNIT_ROUNDOFF) and their messages byte-unchanged; the per-node power-of-two scale_exp handling and mass-sheet/phase reconstruction are byte-preserved. The batched core is numba-njit fastmath=False with no thresholds moved into compiled code. No test files are modified by this WP.
  Max turns: 60

### WP2: Wire channels._exact_total to the batched F_op_grid
  What: Rewire the per-node F_op loop in the engine hot path to call F_op_grid ONCE on the wave-branch node subset, leaving the geometric branch and all downstream outputs bit-unchanged. Do NOT write any tests.
  Where: cogwheel/lensing/chang_refsdal/channels.py (_exact_total); cogwheel/lensing/likelihood.py only if a wiring signature must thread through (expected none).
  How: In _exact_total, keep the per-node branch decision (cancellation_exponent + select_branch) exactly as-is. Partition the w grid into geometric-branch indices (handled per node by geometric_amplification as today) and wave-branch indices. For the wave-branch subset, make a SINGLE call value_wave, orders_wave, converged_wave = F_op_grid(w[wave_idx], source, gamma, beta=beta, kappa=kappa, max_order=max_order) instead of looping scalar F_op; scatter the results back into the total/orders/converged arrays at their indices. Preserve the exact per-node relative-delay carrier total[i] = value_i * exp(-1j * w[i] * t_min) for BOTH branches. Refusals (geometry.LensDomainError, operator.CancellationError) must propagate unswallowed exactly as before so the RB and brute paths refuse symmetrically (a CancellationError raised inside the batched call for any wave node must surface identically to the old per-node raise — do not catch-and-continue). Do not change ChangRefsdalChannels.evaluate's packaging of operator_orders/operator_converged, _physical_kernels, _channel_switch, or exact_transition_channels. Confirm _amplification_coefficients and lnlike produce identical outputs (this is a speed-only change). ARTIFACT NOTE: no DATA_CONTRACTS artifact schema changes (engine internals only), so no producer/consumer reordering is needed.
  Who: Coder
  Dependencies: WP1
  Verification: channels._exact_total performs a single F_op_grid call over the wave-branch node subset (no residual per-node scalar F_op loop on that subset) and per-node geometric_amplification on the geometric subset; the per-node exp(-1j*w*t_min) carrier is applied to both branches; LensDomainError and CancellationError propagate unswallowed and symmetrically. ChangRefsdalChannels.evaluate, _amplification_coefficients, and lnlike return values are unchanged versus the pre-WP1 engine within the certified band. No test files are modified by this WP.
  Max turns: 40

### Professor Inputs
  - Node count is ~100 (not ~1e5); the ~2.3 ms/node splits ~1.9 ms contraction + ~0.4 ms 1F1 kernel, so contraction is ~190 ms of the ~300 ms eval — the dominant, batchable term.
  - Weight-vector reduction (authoritative algebra): v_n[j] = sum over (a,b) with idx(a,b)==j of z_powers[a]*table[n,a,b]*zbar_powers[b], w-independent; per node order-n contribution = length-85 dot v_n.derivs_scaled. ~190x contraction (190 ms -> ~1 ms).
  - Accumulation-order change is SAFE: blocked/dot summation is better-conditioned than the current naive column-then-row loop; for returned points condition = positive_total/|total| < ~9e6 gives perturbation < ~2e-8 relative, ~200x under the 1e-10 target; higher-condition points are already refused, so no certified point flips.
  - Batch EVERYTHING through one path and one certification — do NOT split value-producing and refusal-deciding computations, which would certify one computation while returning another (coherence violation). Re-certify batched-vs-mpmath-oracle at FOP_RTOL=1e-10 on FOP_GRID + the L in [24,48] CERT_LS band, and assert refusal-decision identity (single-vs-batch, zero flips).
  - Predicted floor arithmetic: contraction 190->~2 ms, kernel ~35 ms (NOT batchable — variable n_terms per node + sequential dd recurrence), overhead ~1 ms, non-engine ~70 ms -> ~108 ms lnlike (~2.9x). Gate MS_CEILING = 0.175 s (108 ms x 1.6 margin, arithmetic-derived, replacing the machine-calibrated 0.5 s); raise SPEEDUP_MIN 3.0 -> 8.0 (predicted ~139x over ~15 s brute); lead with structural gates, treat absolute ms as a secondary regression guard.
  - Next lever = Lever B (3D post-contraction surrogate of the smooth O(1) K_a over reduced (w, y', gamma'); kappa eliminated by mass-sheet identity, beta by rotation), deferred to Build 4. It is materially different from the rejected 2D derivative-ladder table because it tabulates the O(1) post-contraction output, not the ~100-decade internal ladder. Lever D (170-dim ODE marching) rejected as slower at 100 nodes; the non-engine ~70 ms becomes the new bottleneck and is named in the change report.
  - Convention traps for the Coder: w is log-spaced (never assume uniform spacing/FFT tricks); n_terms and scale_exp vary per node (per-node ldexp reconstruction, no global rescale); mass-sheet phase reconstruction stays per-node with the node's own w; xi = 8*pi*G*M_L*(1+z_L)/c^3 depends on the sampled M_L so the w grid moves per sample (fine for WP1/WP2, but a hard constraint on any future Lever-B table domain).
  - F010 discipline for the new njit core: self-falsification must use the py_func-chain idiom (patch the batched core AND every njit callee to .py_func) and assert each patched object is a py_func body; perturb _SERIES_TOLERANCE->1.0 and a zeroed half_sum gather and confirm each drives the 1e-10 accuracy gate RED, else the gate is vacuous.

### Domain Test Descriptions
  - BatchedContractionCertificationTestCase (re-certify the accumulation-order change against the independent oracle; Professor-specified). SETUP: exercise F_op_grid on the UNION of (a) the in-domain FOP_GRID sweep (w in {1,10,20,40,50}, sqrt_s in {0.3,0.9}, gamma in {0,0.2}, kappa=0, beta=0, max_order=70; L=w*sqrt_s from 0.3 to 45) and (b) the F005 boundary band CERT_LS: L in linspace(24,48,17) at y=(0.9,0), gamma=0.20, kappa=0 (w=L/0.9). The oracle F_oracle is the 70-dps mpmath oracle (_oracle_fop / _oracle_amplification) built ENTIRELY from mpmath.hyp1f1 and an integer-coefficient (u,v) monomial ladder — it must import nothing from operator.F_op/F_op_grid/channels/geometry (F002 oracle-independence; enforce with the AST import guard idiom already used in the lens suites). OPERATION+EXPECTED: (1) Oracle accuracy — for every grid point where F_op_grid returns (no CancellationError for that node), assert |F_batched - F_oracle|/|F_oracle| <= FOP_RTOL = 1e-10 (UNCHANGED). (2) Refusal-decision identity — for each grid point compare the return-vs-CancellationError decision between F_op_grid called with a single-element array [w] and F_op_grid called with the FULL array containing that w; the per-node decisions must be IDENTICAL with ZERO flips (catches cross-node convergence-state leakage). (3) Single-vs-batch value agreement — where both return, assert |F_single - F_batch|/|F_single| <= 1e-14 (identical code on identical data; any larger gap is cross-node contamination). Across CERT_LS both outcomes must occur (certified at low L, refused at high L — the XOR contract). DIAGNOSTIC: scatter of log10(|F_batched-F_oracle|/|F_oracle|) vs L with the 1e-10 ceiling line (all points below or refused); a boolean single-vs-batch refusal-flag map (all identical); a violation shows as a point above the ceiling that is not refused, or a refusal-flag mismatch.
  - BatchedContractionFalsificationTestCase (F010 self-falsification for the new njit code; Professor-specified). PREAMBLE: numba freezes module globals at compile time, so patching a module-global does NOT reach compiled code — use the py_func-chain idiom: patch the batched contraction njit core AND every njit function it calls to their .py_func bodies for the duration of the patch, and assert each patched object is a py_func body (e.g. it has no `.signatures`) so a future @njit removal can't silently make the chain vacuous. SETUP: pick one in-domain config w=20, y=(0.55,0), gamma=0.20, kappa=0 (L=11, certified); confirm the UNPATCHED F_op_grid is within 1e-10 of the mpmath oracle (gate can go green). OPERATION+EXPECTED — two perturbations, each must drive the accuracy gate RED (|perturbed-oracle|/|oracle| > 1e-10): (a) patch operator._SERIES_TOLERANCE to 1.0 through the py_func chain so the small-term stop fires at order 0-1 and truncates the shear series — at gamma=0.20 this drops a ~4% correction, ~1e8x above the gate; (b) pass a corrupted half_sum (all zeros) into the batched core via the py_func path so every (a,b) reads derivs_scaled[order], collapsing the bilinear form — wrong at any nontrivial source. If either perturbation leaves the gate green, fail with a message that the gate is vacuous or the py_func chain is incomplete (F010). DIAGNOSTIC: print perturbed-vs-oracle relative error for each perturbation; both must exceed 1e-10.
  - FewMsTimingTestCase update (arithmetic-derived gate, NOT machine-calibrated; Professor-specified; owner hot button). SETUP: LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood on the crown four-image config (_CROWN), OMP/MKL/NUMBA threads pinned to 1, JIT-warm with 2 calls before timing. OPERATION: time warm best-of-TIMING_REPEATS lnlike, lnlike_bruteforce, _amplification_coefficients, and the pure _data_term+_norm_term contraction (inputs from the live hot path); print a per-component breakdown (caustic-search, 1F1 kernel/engine, contraction, non-engine, total, speedup). EXPECTED — lead with the machine-INDEPENDENT structural gates: (i) t_brute > SPEEDUP_MIN * t_rb with SPEEDUP_MIN raised 3.0 -> 8.0 (predicted lnlike ~139x over ~15 s brute; 8.0 sits ~17x below the predicted floor, a structural non-retuned advance — the assertion message prints the measured ratio); (ii) the pure contraction is subdominant to the amplification-engine call (existing structural gate, kept). Then the arithmetic-derived absolute regression guard: (iii) t_rb <= MS_CEILING = 0.175 s, whose docstring states the derivation (108 ms predicted floor = contraction ~2 ms + kernel ~35 ms + overhead ~1 ms + non-engine ~70 ms, times a 1.6x margin) and states this is NOT the brief's 10 ms target (that needs Lever B, deferred to Build 4). The absolute ms ceiling is secondary; the printed breakdown lets a regression pinpoint the slipped lever. DIAGNOSTIC: component bar chart — the amplification engine should shrink dramatically and the non-engine path should now be the overall ceiling.
  - Equivalence confirmation (batching changed speed, not physics; Professor-specified). This is primarily a CONFIRMATION that all existing gates stay green at ORIGINAL tolerances with ZERO constant changes, since the single-path design makes existing tests exercise the batched path automatically: BruteForceAgreementTestCase (RB-vs-brute on all 5 _LENS_CONFIGS, near-fold, and waveform-offset) at max(RB_ATOL=1.5, RB_RTOL=1e-2*|bf|); DeterminismTestCase bit-identical repeat; CrownAccuracyAnchorTestCase (RB-vs-brute every config; zero-noise F->1 floor at ZERO_NOISE_TOL=1e-2/RB_FLOOR_REGRESSION=1.5e-2; macro-magnification limit at MACRO_LIMIT_RTOL=1e-8 down to w~1e-12 against the literal closed form 1/sqrt((1-kappa)^2-gamma^2), never built from F_op/channels per F009/F002; near-cusp regression pin; symmetric LensDomainError refusal on a macro saddle); CoarseNodeInterpolationTestCase null-safe production-grid interp at INTERP_NULLSAFE_CEIL=1e-3; NumbaOperatorPreservationTestCase / ContractionCertificationTestCase / OperatorOracleTestCase at RTOL 1e-10 with unchanged refusal grids. PLUS one new one-line assertion: at a representative in-domain point (w=20, y=(0.55,0), gamma=0.20) assert F_op(w,y,gamma) == F_op_grid(np.array([w]),y,gamma) value bit-identical (assertEqual), confirming the scalar entry point delegates to the batched path. EXPECTED: every listed gate passes with no tolerance widened; the new delegation assertion is exact.

